* ✅ /do178c-rust-avionics/  
* ✅ /capability-statement/  
* ✅ /pitch-deck/  
* ✅ /business-card/  
* ❌ /compliance — will 404

### **2.3 Cross-Domain Links (must be absolute)**

| Destination | Required URL |
| :---- | :---- |
| Corporate Hub | https://atelierlogicgroup.com/ |
| Product Hub | https://relulayer.ai/ |
| Capability Statement | https://atelierlogicgroup.com/capability-statement/ |
| SBLO Contact Form | https://atelierlogicgroup.com/\#sblo-form |

### **2.4 Canonical URLs & Sitemaps**

Every page must declare a canonical URL matching the public route, including the trailing slash for directory routes:

* https://atelierlogicgroup.com/  
* https://atelierlogicgroup.com/relulayer/  
* https://atelierlogicgroup.com/capability-statement/  
* https://relulayer.ai/

Sitemaps are generated as sitemap-index.xml referencing sitemap-0.xml and served directly with HTTP 200 OK and text/xml headers.

## **3\. Astro Component Standards**

### **3.1 Printable Documents**

Any page intended for print or PDF export must use **inline or global styles** for @media print and :root rules. Astro's default scoped style transform will strip or hash these rules.

* ✅ \<style is:inline\> — preferred for standalone printable pages (e.g., capability-statement.astro, business-card.astro).  
* ✅ \<style is:global\> — acceptable for layout-injected print overrides (e.g., compliance.astro).  
* ❌ \<style\> (scoped) — will break @media print and :root.

### **3.2 Layout & Schema.org**

* BaseLayout.astro injects global styles via \<style is:global\> and imports src/styles/global.css.  
* The JSON-LD Schema.org block must keep is:inline so it renders as raw JSON.  
* The pageType prop accepts 'corporate' or 'product'; both resolve to the same dark navy theme (\#0B192C).

### **3.3 Footer / Navigation Maintenance**

* Navigation.astro must continue using absolute URLs for all cross-domain links.  
* When adding a new solution page, append it to Footer.astro solutionLinks with a trailing slash.

## **4\. Validation Checklist (mandatory before any commit or deploy)**

Run the verification command locally and fix every failure before opening a PR or deploying:

npm run verify

This executes:

npm run build && npx linkinator ./dist \--recurse --skip 'https://atelierlogicgroup.com\|https://relulayer.ai\|https://fonts.googleapis.com\|mailto:'

### **Manual checklist**

* \[ \] npm run build completes with zero errors.  
* \[ \] npx linkinator ./dist \--recurse reports zero broken links.  
* \[ \] All cross-domain links use absolute URLs (https://...).  
* \[ \] All same-domain links end with /.  
* \[ \] Printable pages use \<style is:inline\> or \<style is:global\> for @media print and :root rules.  
* \[ \] Canonical URLs match the final public route exactly.  
* \[ \] UEI, CAGE, NAICS, PSC, and USPTO serial numbers are unchanged and consistently rendered.

## **5\. CI/CD & Deployment**

### **5.1 Verified Commands**

| Command | Purpose |
| :---- | :---- |
| npm ci | Clean install in CI |
| npm run check | Astro type/lint check |
| npm run build | Static build to dist/ |
| npx linkinator ./dist \--recurse | Link validation |
| npm run verify | Combined build \+ link check |

### **5.2 Deployment Pipelines & Runner Status**

* **CI/CD Daemon (pacificailab):** act\_runner (v0.2.10) running as a system daemon (wsl-deploy-runner) bound to \[ubuntu-latest, ubuntu-22.04, ubuntu-20.04\].  
* **Single Root Workflow:** Deploys both domains from the root repository:  
  * main push → production environment (AWS Lightsail)  
  * workflow\_dispatch → manual production deployment  
  * atelierlogicgroup.com → /var/www/atelierlogicgroup.com/  
  * relulayer.ai → /var/www/relulayer.ai/  
  * Post-deploy: execute update\_nginx\_410.sh, run protect\_intellectual\_property.sh, and reload Nginx.

### **5.3 Environment Secrets**

* LIGHTSAIL\_SSH\_KEY\_\*, LIGHTSAIL\_HOST\_\*, LIGHTSAIL\_USER\_\*  
* CLOUDFLARE\_ZONE\_ID, CLOUDFLARE\_API\_TOKEN

## **6\. Git Commit Workflow**

* Verify the current upstream branch before pushing: git branch \-vv or git status.  
* Do not push directly to main or develop without a PR/merge request.  
* The relulayer-site/ directory is an independent git repository. Commits inside it must be made from the relulayer-site/ working tree and pushed to its own remote.  
* If a CLI push hangs, check the remote URL and branch tracking first; never force-push without explicit authorization.  
* Use clear, descriptive commit messages. Do not commit secrets, .env files, or raw build artifacts (dist/ is ignored).

## **7\. Common Anti-Patterns to Avoid**

* Changing entity identifiers (UEI, CAGE, NAICS, PSC, USPTO serial) without explicit user approval.  
* Using relative cross-domain links (/capability-statement/ from relulayer.ai).  
* Omitting trailing slashes on internal directory routes.  
* Adding scoped \<style\> blocks for @media print rules.  
* Skipping npm run verify before a deployment.  
* Editing files inside relulayer-site/ as if they were part of the root Astro source tree without a separate commit in that repository.  
* Exposing internal SBIR, proposal, or IP material (docs/sbir/, public/docs/SBIR/, QUARANTINE\_DO\_NOT\_USE/, DSIP\_Submission\_\*/, FINAL\_SBIR\_SUBMISSION\_\*/) in public/, dist/, or any deployable output. These directories must stay out of the static build and repository history.